00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:06.040
in the breath of God in birth and breeds out the breath of God in death and generation

57
00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:12.640
after generation, the human race is breathing. And the name that was given to God and the

58
00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:25.920
very ancient times of Moses was Yahweh. This is the meaning of it. Look. Yah. You breathe

59
00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:31.080
out. You breathe in. And that's what the human race is doing all the time. That's why one

60
00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:36.880
of the very important images of the Holy Spirit is the breath of God. That the breath of God

61
00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:45.760
was given to us at the very beginning. Okay. So subject to dying and being born again,

62
00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:52.040
one of the really touching moments I had in Pretoria in South Africa at one stage giving

63
00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:59.960
you a retreat there was that on a particular day in the same hospital on two different levels,

64
00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:05.720
an old man died at 11 in the morning and his grandson was born at exactly 11 o'clock in

65
00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:11.640
the morning as well. The old generation gave back the breath and the new generation drew

66
00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:17.760
it in. And so at his funeral, we had the mother and her little baby and explained there is

67
00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:23.000
a time for everything. And there's a time for the breath to be drawn in and to be given

68
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:29.640
back to God. And considering that the congregation where African they understood perfectly what

69
00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:35.480
we were saying, we said it in Ireland, you'd have to explain yourself 10 times. They understood

